<title>GREECE: Greek/Bund gap shrinks to 365 bps, 270 vs BTP.</title>
<headline>Greek/Bund gap shrinks to 365 bps, 270 vs BTP.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-07-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The spread of Greece's 10-year bond over bunds eased to 365 basis points today from 366 on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The Greek/BTP gap also decreased to 270 basis points from 274 on Wednesday.</p>
<p>		 CPN     MATURITY  YIELDS    SPREADS    PREVIOUS</p>
<p>								    SPREADS</p>
<p>   GREECE    8.80%   25JUN07    9.21%</p>
<p>   GERMANY   6.0%    04JUL07    5.56%	365	366 bps</p>
<p>   FRANCE    5.5%    25APR07    5.42%	379	380 bps</p>
<p>   ITALY     6.75%   01FEB07    6.51%	270	274 bps</p>
<p>   PORTUGAL  6.63%   23FEB07    6.30%	291	293 bps</p>
<p>   SPAIN     7.35%   31MAR07    6.22%	299	301 bps</p>
<p>   UK	  7.25%   07DEC07    7.21%	199	202 bps</p>
<p>   US	  6.63%   15MAY07    6.35%	286	284 bps</p>
<p>All yields are annualised and based on bid prices at 0946 GMT.</p>
<p>--Dimitris Kontogiannis, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
